 Scotch). ~8 bolls ≈ 1,500 modern bottles ATTRIBUTED to the Scotch Whisky Association, not asserted flat. Speyside = 50+ distilleries, over half of Scotland, densest concentration of malt distilleries on earth, ~60% of Scotland's malt (masterofmalt, spiritofspeyside, wikipedia). ~150-152 operating malt distilleries in Scotland (2025, whiskyinvestdirect, wikipedia list). Coffey continuous/column still patented 1830 (grain whisky) vs pot still (single malt) (scotchwhisky.com, wikipedia Aeneas Coffey). Age statement = age of the YOUNGEST whisky in the bottle per SWR2009, applies to vatted single malts (whiskyinvestdirect, dlapiper). Real pull-quote = the 1494 Exchequer Rolls entry itself, a documented primary-source artifact (freediving/coffee precedent — a real record, NOT an invented distiller quote). Pick = Springbank Whisky School, Campbeltown (5-day residential since 2007, class of 6, hands-on every step floor-malting→mashing→distilling→cask-filling→bottling, one of the last distilleries doing all steps on site, exam+certificate, ~£1,400, verified insidethecask/scotchwhisky.com/whiskyadvocate); gate shown honestly = the Springbank certificate is a memento NOT a professional qualification, the recognised ladder is the Chartered Institute of Brewers & Distillers (ex-IBD) General Certificate→Diploma in Distilling (exam-based, industry gold standard, cibd.org.uk) OR Heriot-Watt International Centre for Brewing & Distilling MSc (teaching since 1903, needs a science degree, hw.ac.uk). English path = it's Scotland. Alts labelled: Ireland (English, triple-distilled tradition), Kentucky/Tennessee bourbon (English but a DIFFERENT product — corn, new charred oak), Japan (mostly Japanese). | go-deeper: book = The World Atlas of Whisky, Dave Broom (Hachette canonical title page hachette.co.uk/.../9781784720155, raw search-result URL — used publisher page since openlibrary was un-fetchable; index-verified) + podcast = WhiskyCast, Mark Gillespie (whiskycast.com, world's longest-